# LUL-1664 / LUL-1772 -- entries mirror scripts/pr-tier.mjs's Tier C rules
# exactly (checked against pr-tier.mjs 2026-09-17, current after LUL-1880's
# named-list narrowing) so the two never drift silently apart.
#
# Inert today: GitHub only enforces this once `require_code_owner_review:
# true` is set on rulesets 21050378 (release/next) and 20886790 (main), and
# `@lullwood-code-reviewer` (a GitHub App, per the 2026-09-16 founder
# decision on LUL-1772) has to exist and be installed on this repo before it
# can own anything. Both are founder-only actions, tracked on LUL-1772.
# Until then, this file changes nothing about how PRs merge.
#
# Paths not listed here (app/, components/, lib/ minus the lib/game files
# below, docs/, e2e/, public/, ...) are Tier A/B and intentionally have no
# code owner -- the existing required_approving_review_count: 1 (any
# identity) keeps governing them exactly as it does today.
#
# Known gap: pr-tier.mjs also classifies C by CONTENT, not just path --
# `/(auth|secret|token|credential)/i` matched anywhere in the filename.
# CODEOWNERS only matches paths, so e.g. a new `lib/foo-token-helper.ts`
# would be Tier C to pr-tier.mjs but ownerless here. No CODEOWNERS-side fix
# exists; flagged on LUL-1772, not blocking the rest of this file.

/.github/              @lullwood-code-reviewer
/scripts/              @lullwood-code-reviewer
/engine/               @lullwood-code-reviewer
/app/api/              @lullwood-code-reviewer
/package.json          @lullwood-code-reviewer
